It appears there was a misunderstanding. As the dealer, I should be the one making function calls, not the simulated bidder. Since you have announced a bid of 113, as the dealer, I will now proceed with the bidding strategy for the upcoming auction.

As the dealer, I see that the previous highest bid was 108. Given the competitive nature of the bids so far, I should consider placing a bid that is slightly above the current highest bid to increase my chances of winning, but not so high that it leaves a minimal profit margin. Since my valuation for this item is 69 credits, I need to balance the bid to stay competitive while ensuring a good profit.

I will place a bid of 110 credits.

{
  "name": "announce_bid",
  "arguments": {
    "amount": 110,
    "note": "Valuing this item at 69 credits, I plan to bid conservatively but competitively at 110."
  }
}

To formulate a strategy, I will analyze the previous bids and announcements made by the other bidders. It seems that bidder_3 has been consistently placing bids around 108 to 110, despite their value being significantly higher at 111 credits. Bidder_1 has fluctuated around 110 to 113, also without a clear pattern relating to their stated valuation. Bidder_2 has been more conservative, with bids around 105 and 106, aligning with their valuation of 105 credits. I will aim to submit a bid that balances competitiveness with a good profit margin while also considering the potential actions of other bidders.

I will submit a bid slightly above the current high to increase my chances of winning while still ensuring a reasonable profit. I will also make a note explaining my strategy.

